    359  6d58							; ------------------------------------------------------------ One Key Play
    360  6d58							; CRSR DOWN or CRSR RIGHT (A = 1 / 2: which) pressed, ONE KEY PLAY on: the
    361  6d58							; phrase's next step sounds. PENTATONIC PAIRS: two notes of the key's
    362  6d58							; pentatonic scale, one apart (a third or a fourth), across the overlay's two
    363  6d58							; octaves. CHORD NOTES: one note of the chord (the keys held or latched),
    364  6d58							; over two octaves. EACH PRESS CUTS the last step or lets it RING ON (until
    365  6d58							; the next). The notes sound while either key is down (latch: until the next
    366  6d58							; press).
    367  6d58				   OkpPress
    368  6d58					      subroutine
    369  6d58		       0d 86 c8 	      ora	okpDown
    370  6d5b		       8d 86 c8 	      sta	okpDown
    371  6d5e		       ad 83 c8 	      lda	okpRing	; RINGS ON: the last step stays
    372  6d61		       f0 15		      beq	.cut
    373  6d63		       ad 87 c8 	      lda	okpCount
    374  6d66		       f0 10		      beq	.cut
    375  6d68		       ad 88 c8 	      lda	okpNotes
    376  6d6b		       8d 8a c8 	      sta	okpNotes+2
    377  6d6e		       ad 89 c8 	      lda	okpNotes+1
    378  6d71		       8d 8b c8 	      sta	okpNotes+3
